CON-14: book LID releases as a negative BMP removal instead of creating mass

surfqual_getWashoff() turns the step's washoff load into a concentration over
the pre-LID runoff volume vOut1 and exports it over the post-LID volume vOut2
(surface runoff + LID drains). The difference vOut1 - vOut2 was booked as
infiltration / BMP removal only when positive. When the LIDs release stored
water (vOut2 > vOut1, typically an underdrain after the storm), the surplus
was exported with that concentration and no ledger term paid for it, while
the same water's mass had been counted as BMP removal when it was captured.
Book the signed difference: a release reduces the BMP removal. Exported
loads and concentrations do not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-14_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c b/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c
index 893b975..69abc65 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/surfqual.c
@@ -339,16 +339,18 @@ void surfqual_getWashoff(int subcatchIndex, double runoff, double tStep)
         //     the categories physically distinct and closes the mass balance.
         if (Subcatch[subcatchIndex].lidArea > 0.0)
         {
+            //     (vLost < 0 when the LIDs release more water than the
+            //      subcatchment generates; the mass it carries is booked
+            //      as a negative BMP removal, i.e. a return from storage)
             vLost = vOut1 - vOut2;
-            if (vLost < 0.0) vLost = 0.0;
-            vInfil = MIN(vLidInfil, vLost);
+            vInfil = MIN(vLidInfil, MAX(vLost, 0.0));
 
             massLoad = cOut * vInfil * Pollut[p].mcf;
             if (massLoad > 0.0)
                 massbal_updateLoadingTotals(INFIL_LOAD, p, massLoad);
 
             massLoad = cOut * (vLost - vInfil) * Pollut[p].mcf;
-            if (massLoad > 0.0)
+            if (massLoad != 0.0)
                 massbal_updateLoadingTotals(BMP_REMOVAL_LOAD, p, massLoad);
         }
 
